  "headword": "{絶|た}え{間|ま}なく",
  "reading": "たえまなく",
  "part_of_speech": "adverb",
  "gloss": "incessantly; ceaselessly; without pause",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "incessantly; ceaselessly; without pause; continuously",
      "explanation": "Without any break or interruption. Describes an action or state that continues uninterrupted."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "16251_taemanaku_ex1",
      "japanese": "{雨|あめ}が{絶|た}え{間|ま}なく{降|ふ}っている。",
      "english": "The rain is falling ceaselessly.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "16251_taemanaku_ex2",
      "japanese": "{車|くるま}が{絶|た}え{間|ま}なく{通|とお}り{過|す}ぎる。",
      "english": "Cars pass by without pause.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "16251_taemanaku_ex3",
      "japanese": "{絶|た}え{間|ま}なく{努力|どりょく}を{続|つづ}けたおかげで、ついに{夢|ゆめ}が{叶|かな}った。",
      "english": "Thanks to my ceaseless efforts, my dream finally came true.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "USAGE:\n{絶|た}え{間|ま}なく is the adverbial form of {絶|た}え{間|ま}ない (unceasing). It modifies verbs and emphasizes the continuous, unbroken nature of an action. Somewhat literary.\n\nWORD FORMATION:\n{絶|た}える (to cease) + {間|ま} (interval) + なく (without) — literally \"without a gap of ceasing.\"\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {絶|た}え{間|ま}なく{続|つづ}く: to continue ceaselessly\n- {絶|た}え{間|ま}なく{降|ふ}る: to rain without pause\n- {絶|た}え{間|ま}ない{努力|どりょく}: ceaseless effort\n- {絶|た}え{間|ま}ない{流|なが}れ: an unbroken flow",
